  "workedExample": "A creator earns $9,000 of gross YouTube revenue and claims $2,000 of deductible gear, editing software and AI tool subscriptions, leaving $7,000 of net profit. Self-employment tax applies to 92.35% of that profit ($6,464.50) at the 15.3% rate, resulting in $989.07 of self-employment tax. Because the $7,000 profit remains below the $16,100 standard deduction, federal income tax is zero if the creator has no other income. If that creator also earns a $60,000 salary from an outside employer, the YouTube profit stacks into the 22% federal tax bracket, increasing the total tax bill.",
